<% content_for :title, "How it works and what it costs | Norman Simplified" %>
<% content_for :description, "Start with a two-week Workflow Review for $4,500. See what is included, implementation prices, and what happens next." %>

<main class="ns-how">
  <section class="ns-section ns-how__hero" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <div class="ns-container">
      <p class="sn-eyebrow">Scope before work</p>
      <h1 id="how-title" class="t-display ns-how__title">Start with a Workflow Review</h1>
      <p class="ns-lead">Workflow Review. $4,500 fixed fee. Two weeks.</p>
      <ul class="ns-how__list ns-review-scope">
        <li>Four conversations with the people who do the work</li>
        <li>Three recurring processes compared: where the time goes and what it costs</li>
        <li>One recommended first change, in writing</li>
        <li>A budget range for making that change, with the assumptions shown</li>
        <li>A plain go or no-go recommendation</li>
        <li>A 45-minute walkthrough of the report</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="ns-lead">The usual first step is a Workflow Review. The report is yours whether or not you continue. $2,000 of the fee is credited toward any implementation project with Norman Simplified that starts within 60 days.</p>
      <div class="ns-actions">
        <%= link_to "Request a call", studio_contact_path(interest: "audit"), data: { controller: "analytics", action: "click->analytics#track", analytics_event_param: "cta_clicked", analytics_cta_param: "request_a_call", analytics_location_param: "hero", analytics_interest_param: "audit" }, class: "sn-btn sn-btn--primary sn-btn--lg" %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ns-section ns-how__overview" aria-labelledby="three-lanes">
    <div class="ns-container">
      <header class="ns-section-heading">
        <h2 id="three-lanes" class="t-heading">What happens after the review</h2>
        <p class="ns-lead">You can stop, do the work in-house, or ask for a separately scoped, fixed-price implementation. If you already know what you need, we can discuss it on the call.</p>
      </header>
      <dl class="ns-how__lanes">
        <div>
          <dt><a class="ns-text-link" href="#adopt">Tools and training</a></dt>
          <dd><strong>$3,500 fixed fee.</strong> A written tool recommendation. Staff rollout is a separate $8,500 fixed-fee project.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt><a class="ns-text-link" href="#automate">Workflow automation</a></dt>
          <dd><strong>Starts at $7,500.</strong> One recurring process connected across your tools. Your written proposal sets the fixed fee before work begins.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt><a class="ns-text-link" href="#build">Custom software</a></dt>
          <dd><strong>Starts at $18,000.</strong> Software for a process that has outgrown a spreadsheet or an old app. Your written proposal sets the fixed fee before work begins.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="adopt" class="ns-section ns-how__lane" aria-labelledby="adopt-title">
    <div class="ns-container ns-editorial-grid">
      <header class="ns-section-heading">
        <h2 id="adopt-title" class="t-heading">Tools and training</h2>
        <p class="ns-lead">For a company that needs a decision and a shared practice, not a new application.</p>
        <div class="ns-actions"><%= link_to "Request a call", studio_contact_path(interest: "adopt"), data: { controller: "analytics", action: "click->analytics#track", analytics_event_param: "cta_clicked", analytics_cta_param: "request_a_call", analytics_location_param: "lanes", analytics_interest_param: "adopt" }, class: "sn-btn sn-btn--primary sn-btn--md" %></div>
      </header>
      <div class="ns-how__offers">
        <article class="ns-how__offer ns-prose">
          <h3 class="t-heading">Tool recommendation</h3>
          <p class="ns-how__price">$3,500 fixed fee · 10 days</p>
          <p><strong>What you get:</strong> A memo that names which of ChatGPT, Claude, Copilot, or Gemini to buy, who gets a seat, what is off limits, and the order of the next 90 days. Plus a 45-minute walkthrough.</p>
          <p><strong>Credit:</strong> $1,500 applies to a Staff rollout or Workflow automation project that starts within 60 days.</p>
          <p>You buy the tools directly from the vendor.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="ns-how__offer ns-prose">
          <h3 class="t-heading">Staff rollout</h3>
          <p class="ns-how__price">$8,500 fixed fee · 3 weeks · up to 30 people</p>
          <p><strong>What you get:</strong> A one-page use policy, two live sessions split by role, a prompt pack for three jobs your staff already do, and ten business days of follow-up questions.</p>
          <p><strong>Over 30 people:</strong> Quoted separately. The proposal sets the scope and price.</p>
          <p><strong>What usually comes next:</strong> Monthly working sessions, or a Workflow automation project if the same task keeps recurring.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="ns-how__offer ns-prose">
          <h3 class="t-heading">Monthly working sessions</h3>
          <p class="ns-how__price">$2,500 a month</p>
          <p>Two live hours, plus a look at what staff actually tried between sessions.</p>
          <p>Month to month. Cancel before the next month.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="automate" class="ns-section ns-how__lane" aria-labelledby="automate-title">
    <div class="ns-container ns-editorial-grid">
      <header class="ns-section-heading">
        <h2 id="automate-title" class="t-heading">Workflow automation</h2>
        <p class="ns-lead">For a workflow you can already describe step by step.</p>
        <div class="ns-actions"><%= link_to "Request a call", studio_contact_path(interest: "automate"), data: { controller: "analytics", action: "click->analytics#track", analytics_event_param: "cta_clicked", analytics_cta_param: "request_a_call", analytics_location_param: "lanes", analytics_interest_param: "automate" }, class: "sn-btn sn-btn--primary sn-btn--md" %></div>
      </header>
      <div class="ns-how__offers">
        <article class="ns-how__offer ns-prose">
          <h3 class="t-heading">Workflow automation</h3>
          <p class="ns-how__price">Starts at $7,500 · about 3 weeks</p>
          <p>Your written proposal sets the fixed fee before work begins.</p>
          <p><strong>What you get:</strong> One recurring process connected across your tools, a named owner on your team, and a one-page guide to running it. I use Zapier, Make, or n8n when it fits the work.</p>
          <p>I pick the tool based on volume and who has to maintain it after I leave.</p>
          <p><strong>What it is not:</strong> A new application with its own database and logins. That is custom software.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="ns-how__offer ns-prose">
          <h3 class="t-heading">Automation support</h3>
          <p class="ns-how__price">$1,500 a month</p>
          <p>About two hours of maintenance and small edits each month.</p>
          <p>If the process needs a database or more complex recovery from failures, I will recommend a separately scoped Pilot.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="build" class="ns-section ns-how__lane" aria-labelledby="build-title">
    <div class="ns-container ns-editorial-grid">
      <header class="ns-section-heading">
        <h2 id="build-title" class="t-heading">Custom software</h2>
        <p class="ns-lead">For a process that needs its own software. The <%= link_to "Examples page", studio_ai_integration_path, class: "ns-inline-link" %> shows possible projects. A Pilot is the usual first implementation.</p>
        <div class="ns-actions"><%= link_to "Request a call", studio_contact_path(interest: "build"), data: { controller: "analytics", action: "click->analytics#track", analytics_event_param: "cta_clicked", analytics_cta_param: "request_a_call", analytics_location_param: "lanes", analytics_interest_param: "build" }, class: "sn-btn sn-btn--primary sn-btn--md" %></div>
      </header>
      <div class="ns-how__offers">
        <article class="ns-how__offer ns-prose">
          <h3 class="t-heading">Pilot</h3>
          <p class="ns-how__price">Starts at $18,000 · 3–4 weeks</p>
          <p>Your written proposal sets the fixed fee before work begins.</p>
          <p>One process connected to the system your team uses. We agree how to judge the result before kickoff.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="ns-how__offer ns-prose">
          <h3 class="t-heading">Full integration</h3>
          <p class="ns-how__price">Starts at $36,000 · 6–8 weeks</p>
          <p>Your written proposal sets the fixed fee before work begins.</p>
          <p>A complete workflow connected to your tools, tested against examples from your own work. See the <%= link_to "Examples page", studio_ai_integration_path, class: "ns-inline-link" %>.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="ns-how__offer ns-prose">
          <h3 class="t-heading">Existing app repair</h3>
          <p>Starts at $40,000. Your written proposal sets the fixed fee before work begins, after a look at the codebase. See <%= link_to "Existing app repair on the Examples page", studio_ai_integration_path, class: "ns-inline-link" %>.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="ns-how__offer ns-prose">
          <h3 class="t-heading">After it is live</h3>
          <p>Ongoing operations support starts at $6,500 a month. Your written proposal sets the fixed fee before work begins. You can also run the software with the handoff notes.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ns-section ns-process" aria-labelledby="weeks-title">
    <div class="ns-container ns-editorial-grid">
      <header class="ns-section-heading"><h2 id="weeks-title" class="t-heading">What the weeks look like</h2></header>
      <ol class="ns-process__steps" role="list">
        <li><span class="t-label ns-process__number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><p>You send the workflow through the form. I reply by email within two business days.</p></li>
        <li><span class="t-label ns-process__number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><p>A 25-minute call to discuss the work and whether I can help.</p></li>
        <li><span class="t-label ns-process__number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><p>A written scope: price, duration, what is included, what is not, and how we will judge the result.</p></li>
        <li><span class="t-label ns-process__number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><p>Half to start. Work begins when access is available.</p></li>
        <li><span class="t-label ns-process__number" aria-hidden="true">05</span><p>A walkthrough of the work. You decide whether to stop, manage it in-house, or scope the next piece.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ns-section" aria-labelledby="terms-title">
    <div class="ns-container ns-editorial-grid">
      <header class="ns-section-heading"><h2 id="terms-title" class="t-heading">Money and access</h2></header>
      <ul class="ns-how__list">
        <li>Projects: half to start, half when the agreed scope ships</li>
        <li>Monthly plans: paid at the start of the month</li>
        <li>If system access is delayed, we agree a new start date</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="ns-container ns-section">
    <%= link_to "Request a call", studio_contact_path, data: { controller: "analytics", action: "click->analytics#track", analytics_event_param: "cta_clicked", analytics_cta_param: "request_a_call", analytics_location_param: "cta" }, class: "sn-btn sn-btn--primary sn-btn--lg" %>
  </div>
</main>
